<title>FRANCE: Paris airports postal traffic drops in January.</title>
<headline>Paris airports postal traffic drops in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle (CDG) and Orly, handled 11,895 tonnes of postal traffic in January 1997, a decline of 2.4 percent on the same 1996 month the previous year, Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The number of flights wholly dedicated to postal traffic totalled 721 an increase of 14.1 percent on January 1996. -- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
